## Linked Issues

**Issue #292: axi_pkg::LenWidth not compatible with vivado IP packager**
Since commit fe4e020 the typedef `axi_pkg::burst_t` now relies on a Verilog parameter `BurstWidth`. In Occamy emulation these typedefs are used at the ports of a custom packaged Vivado IP. But Vivado requires that "the IP ports are contained within the port description of the HDL file". So custom Vivado IPs can't use `axi_pkg::burst_t` at their top anymore. A possible fix is to define the typedef with a numerical value and then the parameter based on the `$size` of this typedef. See proposition in commit d2f98d6.
